body:
Interactive game ads (Angry Birds, Minesweeper, Luigi's Mansion, Mario Kart, Simon Says, Memory Match) were effectively invisible on desktop due to three compounding issues.

## Changes

- **Viewport overflow** — `getRandomPosition()` used a 250px Y offset, but game popups are 350–450px tall. Increased to 450px with `Math.max(0)` guard for small windows.
- **Stuck-ad timer** — 10s safety timer (designed for off-screen mobile ads) was removing game ads before completion. Extended to 30s for interactive mechanisms.
- **Spawn probability** — Games were 6/26 entries (~23%). Added 40% weighted selection for interactive mechanisms, bringing effective rate to ~63%.
- **Shared constant** — Extracted `INTERACTIVE_MECHANISMS` array used by both spawn weighting and timeout logic.

```javascript
// Before: games render below viewport on 900px-tall screens
// maxY = 900 - 250 = 650; popup at y=650 with 400px height → bottom at 1050px (off-screen)
function getRandomPosition() {
    const maxX = window.innerWidth - 350;
    const maxY = window.innerHeight - 250;
    ...
}

// After: accounts for full popup height
function getRandomPosition(popupHeight) {
    const estimatedHeight = popupHeight || 450;
    const maxX = Math.max(0, window.innerWidth - 350);
    const maxY = Math.max(0, window.innerHeight - estimatedHeight);
    ...
}
```

All 23 ad mechanisms verified rendering correctly at 1280×900 in headless Chromium.
